{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789966473,"nonce":"BeesbOEldRhOxMiz2w6TXqDp0n4=","title":"An outlined region with an aggregate live-in is refused by the LLVM entry ABI","message":"The region outlined for an interpreted frame becomes a function whose parameters are the frame's live-ins. When one of them is a multi-field struct that is not a growable list header (a tuple, an iterator state), llvm_entry_abi_supported refuses the region and promote_outlined_region logs \"LLVM compile failed: ... has an unsupported LLVM entry ABI\"; the frame stays in the Cranelift region for the rest of the call.\n\nSeen on spectral-norm (speed kernel) with ZYPY_LLVM=1 ZYNTAX_OSR_TRACE=1:\n\n    Recompiling HirId(71169) (eval_times_u$resume0) at tier 1 (Some(Optimized))\n    LLVM compile failed: llvm compile_function failed: Backend error: eval_times_u$resume0 has an unsupported LLVM entry ABI\n\nThe region's signature (ZYNTAX_DUMP_HIR_DIR, fn-eval_times_u_resume0-tier1.hir):\n\n    @eval_times_u$resume0(i64, i64, { i64, *opaque(DynamicBox) }, *opaque(DynamicBox), i64, %List{...}, *%List{...}, *opaque(DynamicBox), *opaque(DynamicBox)) -\u003e %List{...}\n\nThe { i64, *DynamicBox } live-in travels by address in the frame (is_held_by_reference) and the Cranelift region takes it that way; the LLVM entry could take it as a pointer parameter and load it, the way compile_osr_helper already loads a held-by-reference live-in from the frame. Until then the check should run before the region is queued, so a refusal is not a failed compile on the broker.","files":null}]}